      {
        "prompt": "A bond’s fixed annual payment stays the same while its purchase price falls. What happens to its current yield (annual payment divided by price)?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "mm-yield",
            "label": "It stays the same regardless of price."
          },
          {
            "id": "mm-treas",
            "label": "It becomes a guaranteed trading profit."
          },
          {
            "id": "mm-rates",
            "label": "It must fall because the price fell."
          },
          {
            "id": "mm-bond",
            "label": "It rises because the same payment is divided by a lower price."
          }
        ],
        "explanation": "Current yield rises when the price falls and the fixed annual payment stays the same. For example, $5 divided by $100 is 5%; $5 divided by $80 is 6.25%. This is not a guarantee of total return."
